---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const lastUpdated = 'November 2026';
---
<Base
  title="Privacy Policy — Lex Research"
  description="Lex Research privacy policy: how we collect, use, and protect your personal data, including information about cookies and Google Analytics."
  keywords="privacy policy, data protection, Lex Research, cookies, GDPR">

  <!-- Hero -->
  <div class="bg-gradient-to-br from-slate-900 via-slate-800 to-slate-900 text-white py-14 sm:py-20">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 text-center">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 bg-amber-500/10 border border-amber-500/20 text-amber-400 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest px-4 py-2 rounded-full mb-6">
        Legal
      </div>
      <h1 class="serif text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold mb-4 leading-tight">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="text-slate-400 text-sm">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Content -->
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-12 sm:py-20">

    <!-- Intro -->
    <div class="bg-amber-50 border border-amber-200 rounded-2xl p-5 sm:p-6 mb-10 flex gap-4">
      <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-amber-600 flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M13 16h-1v-4h-1m1-4h.01M21 12a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z"/></svg>
      <p class="text-sm text-amber-800 leading-relaxed">
        Lex Research ("we", "us", "our") is committed to protecting your privacy. This policy explains what data we collect when you use <strong>lexresearch.org</strong>, how we use it, and your rights regarding that data.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-10 text-slate-700">

      <!-- 1 -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="serif text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4 pb-2 border-b border-stone-200">1. Who We Are</h2>
        <p class="text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed">
          Lex Research is an open-access academic journal publishing peer-reviewed research in international law, human rights, humanitarian law, and comparative legal studies. The journal is founded and operated by <a href="/lamia-akhter" class="text-amber-700 hover:text-amber-900 font-medium">Lamia Akhter</a>. For all privacy-related enquiries, contact us at <a href="mailto:info@lexresearch.org" class="text-amber-700 hover:text-amber-900 font-medium">info@lexresearch.org</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- 2 -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="serif text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4 pb-2 border-b border-stone-200">2. Data We Collect</h2>
        <div class="space-y-4 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed">
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-1">2.1 Information you give us</h3>
            <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1 text-slate-600 ml-2">
              <li>Name and email address when you create an account or contact us</li>
              <li>Username and password (stored securely, never in plain text)</li>
              <li>Article content, abstracts, and biographical information submitted for publication</li>
              <li>Messages sent to us via the contact form or email</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-1">2.2 Information collected automatically</h3>
            <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1 text-slate-600 ml-2">
              <li>Pages visited, time spent, and referring URLs (via Google Analytics)</li>
              <li>Device type, browser, and approximate geographic location (country/city level)</li>
              <li>IP address (anonymised by Google Analytics)</li>
              <li>Session cookies necessary for account login</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- 3 -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="serif text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4 pb-2 border-b border-stone-200">3. How We Use Your Data</h2>
        <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-stone-200">
          <table class="w-full text-sm">
            <thead class="bg-stone-50 border-b border-stone-200">
              <tr>
                <th class="text-left px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-slate-800">Purpose</th>
                <th class="text-left px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-slate-800">Legal Basis</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody class="divide-y divide-stone-100">
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-3 text-slate-700">Managing your author account</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-slate-500">Contract / legitimate interest</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-3 text-slate-700">Publishing submitted articles</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-slate-500">Contract with the author</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-3 text-slate-700">Responding to contact enquiries</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-slate-500">Legitimate interest</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-3 text-slate-700">Analysing site usage to improve content</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-slate-500">Legitimate interest (Google Analytics)</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-3 text-slate-700">Security and fraud prevention</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-slate-500">Legitimate interest</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm text-slate-500 mt-3">We do <strong class="text-slate-700">not</strong> sell, rent, or trade your personal data to any third party.</p>
      </section>

      <!-- 4 -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="serif text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4 pb-2 border-b border-stone-200">4. Cookies</h2>
        <div class="space-y-3 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed">
          <p>We use the following cookies:</p>
          <div class="space-y-2">
            <div class="bg-stone-50 border border-stone-200 rounded-xl p-4">
              <div class="font-semibold text-slate-800 text-sm mb-1">Session cookie</div>
              <p class="text-slate-500 text-sm">Required to keep you logged in to your author account. Deleted when you sign out or close your browser.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-stone-50 border border-stone-200 rounded-xl p-4">
              <div class="font-semibold text-slate-800 text-sm mb-1">Google Analytics cookies (_ga, _gid, _gat)</div>
              <p class="text-slate-500 text-sm">Used to measure how visitors interact with the site. Data is aggregated and anonymised. You can opt out via <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" class="text-amber-700 hover:text-amber-900">Google's opt-out tool</a>.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="text-slate-500 text-sm">We do not use advertising cookies or sell cookie data.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- 5 -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="serif text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4 pb-2 border-b border-stone-200">5. Third-Party Services</h2>
        <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
          <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-amber-500 font-bold flex-shrink-0">—</span><span><strong class="text-slate-800">Google Analytics (Google LLC)</strong> — website usage analytics. Data may be processed in the USA under Google's standard contractual clauses.</span></li>
          <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-amber-500 font-bold flex-shrink-0">—</span><span><strong class="text-slate-800">Cloudflare</strong> — hosting, DNS, and security. Cloudflare processes request data to protect the site from attacks.</span></li>
          <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-amber-500 font-bold flex-shrink-0">—</span><span><strong class="text-slate-800">Google Fonts</strong> — typography. Your browser may send a request to Google's servers when loading fonts.</span></li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- 6 -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="serif text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4 pb-2 border-b border-stone-200">6. Data Retention</h2>
        <ul class="space-y-1 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-600 list-disc list-inside ml-2">
          <li>Account data is retained for as long as your account is active</li>
          <li>Published articles remain on the site indefinitely as part of the academic record</li>
          <li>Contact messages are retained for up to 2 years</li>
          <li>Google Analytics data is retained for 26 months (Google's default)</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- 7 -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="serif text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4 pb-2 border-b border-stone-200">7. Your Rights</h2>
        <p class="text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed mb-3">Depending on your jurisdiction, you may have the right to:</p>
        <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-3">
          {[
            ['Access', 'Request a copy of the personal data we hold about you'],
            ['Correction', 'Ask us to correct inaccurate data'],
            ['Deletion', 'Request deletion of your account and personal data'],
            ['Portability', 'Receive your data in a portable format'],
            ['Objection', 'Object to processing based on legitimate interest'],
            ['Withdrawal', 'Withdraw consent at any time where processing is consent-based'],
          ].map(([title, desc]) => (
            <div class="bg-stone-50 border border-stone-200 rounded-xl p-4">
              <div class="font-semibold text-slate-800 text-sm mb-0.5">{title}</div>
              <p class="text-slate-500 text-sm">{desc}</p>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm text-slate-500 mt-4">To exercise any of these rights, email us at <a href="mailto:info@lexresearch.org" class="text-amber-700 hover:text-amber-900 font-medium">info@lexresearch.org</a>. We will respond within 30 days.</p>
      </section>

      <!-- 8 -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="serif text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4 pb-2 border-b border-stone-200">8. Children's Privacy</h2>
        <p class="text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed">
          Lex Research is an academic journal intended for adults. We do not knowingly collect data from anyone under the age of 16. If you believe a minor has submitted personal data to us, please contact us and we will delete it promptly.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- 9 -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="serif text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4 pb-2 border-b border-stone-200">9. Changes to This Policy</h2>
        <p class="text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed">
          We may update this policy from time to time. The "last updated" date at the top of this page will reflect any changes. Continued use of the site after changes constitutes acceptance of the updated policy.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- 10 -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="serif text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4 pb-2 border-b border-stone-200">10. Contact</h2>
        <p class="text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed">
          For any privacy-related questions or requests, please contact:<br/>
          <a href="mailto:info@lexresearch.org" class="text-amber-700 hover:text-amber-900 font-medium">info@lexresearch.org</a><br/>
          Lex Research Journal — <a href="/about" class="text-amber-700 hover:text-amber-900">lexresearch.org/about</a>
        </p>
      </section>

    </div>

    <!-- Footer nav -->
    <div class="mt-14 pt-8 border-t border-stone-200 flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-3 items-center justify-between">
      <p class="text-xs text-stone-400">© 2026 Lex Research Journal. All rights reserved.</p>
      <a href="/terms-and-conditions" class="text-sm font-medium text-amber-700 hover:text-amber-900 transition-colors">
        Terms &amp; Conditions →
      </a>
    </div>

  </div>
</Base>
